  faqs: [
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor in Alappuzha?", answer: "Send IB Gram the programme, subject, level and exam series, and we put together a shortlist built from tutors who have genuinely taught that exact course. Location carries no weight here, since no school in Alappuzha district runs the IB at all, so syllabus fit does the whole job before a lesson time gets confirmed against your evenings. A free trial class always comes first, and a different tutor gets suggested if the first pairing does not work." },
    { question: "Are Cambridge and Edexcel IGCSE both covered for Alappuzha students?", answer: "Both, yes, delivered as online tuition rather than a visit to the house, since neither board runs directly through a school in the district. A Cambridge candidate is matched by code and tier, Mathematics 0580 Extended or Chemistry 0620 among the common ones; an Edexcel candidate by specification and Foundation or Higher tier, using each board's own past papers throughout." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Alappuzha?", answer: "They do not. That kind of visit happens only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; everywhere else, Alappuzha included, a lesson runs live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard standing in for the desk a visiting tutor would otherwise use. It is genuine tuition from your own home, just not a knock at the door." },
    { question: "What does an IB or IGCSE tutor in Alappuzha cost?", answer: "Programme and level, the subject itself, session length, and how recently the tutor taught that syllabus all decide the fee, fixed for your match before the trial begins and unchanged after. HL Diploma work generally runs higher than IGCSE Core. Online delivery removes travel from the equation entirely, and there is no long-term contract to sign." },
    { question: "Which schools in Alappuzha actually offer IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None at present. Every school across Alappuzha district runs the Kerala State Board, CBSE or a smaller CISCE syllabus. The nearest confirmed IB and Cambridge IGCSE options sit roughly 62 kilometres north in Kochi, including The Choice School in Ambalamugal and Global Public School in Thiruvankulam." },
    { question: "Our family runs a houseboat or resort. Why do so many like us ask about IB or IGCSE?", answer: "It usually comes down to daily contact with international guests rather than any complaint about local schools. Houseboat operators and resort managers along Alappuzha's backwaters and coast often want their own children holding a qualification recognised well beyond Kerala, and with no local school offering either curriculum, online tutoring or a distance school becomes the practical route from day one." },
    { question: "My child was already studying a British curriculum in the Gulf. Can a tutor pick that up in Alappuzha?", answer: "Yes, and it is a request we see often, given how many Alappuzha households have a member working in the Gulf or coming off years at sea in the merchant navy. A tutor gets matched to the exact board, level and syllabus a child was already following, so tutoring carries on that path rather than starting again." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial before we commit to anything?", answer: "Always. A real topic from your child's own syllabus gets worked through with the tutor online, at no cost and no obligation to continue afterward. A short plan for the first month follows the trial, and from there you can carry on as is, ask for changes, or try a different tutor entirely." },
    { question: "Will a tutor write part of an Internal Assessment for my child?", answer: "No, not under any circumstance. Support covers picking a workable research question, unpacking exactly what a criterion is looking for, sanity-checking a data-collection plan, and giving honest feedback on drafts. The assessed work stays entirely the student's, since writing or rewriting it would breach IB integrity rules." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects does IB Gram cover for an Alappuzha family?", answer: "The subjects our small Diploma cohort connected to Alappuzha actually needs: both Maths routes at HL and SL, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, alongside Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance." },
    { question: "Do you tutor MYP and PYP students too, not only the Diploma?", answer: "Both get full attention. MYP sessions for Alappuzha students generally focus on criterion-based writing across the sciences and languages, plus keeping a Personal Project journal on track; PYP sessions build reading, writing and number confidence, working toward the research skills an eventual Exhibition will demand." },
    { question: "Is online tutoring genuinely enough without a local school to compare it against?", answer: "Given that Alappuzha has no local specialist at all for either curriculum, it is closer to the only real option than a fallback. A shared whiteboard, live past papers on screen and recorded worked examples cover most of what a tutor seated next to your child would otherwise do, while opening the field to specialists teaching right across India, not only Kerala." },
    { question: "How does IB Gram verify tutors for Alappuzha students?", answer: "Qualifications, how recently a tutor has taught the precise subject and level, and their handling of assessment criteria all get checked before any family is introduced. With no local school to compare against, genuinely recent experience with the syllabus takes priority over a confident generalist, and the trial class is where a family confirms it directly." },
    { question: "When should tutoring actually start for an Alappuzha student?", answer: "Right at the beginning of the course works best, Grade 9 for IGCSE or Class 11 for the Diploma, leaving time to fix foundations before internal exams, IA deadlines and predicted grades all arrive close together. A later start, even in the final year, can still help provided sessions stay tightly focused on the highest-value topics and past papers." },
    { question: "We are considering a move from the State Board or CBSE to IGCSE. What actually needs work?", answer: "Usually exam technique rather than content. Command words such as explain, evaluate and justify need direct teaching, and habits around coursework or IA planning need building from nothing, since a State Board or CBSE education rarely calls for either. Spending a school holiday on exactly this before the switch tends to pay off." },
    { question: "Can lessons run on weekends or evenings for an Alappuzha household?", answer: "Yes, most families here book weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings. Scheduling accounts for both monsoons, when an earlier evening slot often suits families better, and for boat-race week each August, when local roads and routines shift noticeably. Adding a second weekly slot ahead of mocks or an exam sitting is simple since nothing depends on travel." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit for us?", answer: "You say so, and a different tutor gets arranged. Reviews with families happen every few weeks specifically to catch a mismatch early, rather than letting a child persist with someone who is not working out. There is no long contract in place, so pausing or stopping carries no cost." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any Alappuzha school, or with the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No, not with any school named on this page, and not with the International Baccalaureate Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education or Pearson Edexcel either. Place and school names here only describe where families in Alappuzha genuinely study, and every tutor works to that school's calendar and the relevant board's published syllabus." },
  ],

